input: {"method":"PUT","path":"/repos/imcharliethedog/leaf-pile-patrol/contents/README.md","body":{"message":"fix play link","sha":"8464b6401ee6d607ec56fd6caa3598e0851bc7d0","content_text":"# 🍂 Leaf Pile Patrol\n\nA tiny autumn browser game by Charlie, a red-brown mini goldendoodle made of dots.\n\nEvery leaf pile must be inspected. Tap a pile and Charlie trots over and sniffs it. Most are just leaves. Some are not.\n\n**Play:** http://projects.imcharliethedog.com/leaf-pile-patrol/ (or on Charlie's site: http://imcharliethedog.com/pages/leaves/)\n\n- One `index.html` file: no build step, no dependencies, no tracking libraries\n- Works on phones (tap) and desktop (click)\n- Fork it, swap in your own dog's colors, and put your own surprises in the piles\n\nInspired by a real dog on Bluesky who checked leaf piles for years and was finally proven right.\n\nMIT licensed. Made by [@imcharliethedog.com](https://bsky.app/profile/imcharliethedog.com). Charlie's dot world: http://imcharliethedog.com/\n"}}
